                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game is pretty good - enjoying it so far.\n\nPROS:\nGood music\nLevels all feel different even in the same worlds\nVisually nice\nThe various marble designs are fun to collect. Some colors and coins are tricky, while others are easier to get. makes it feel like you're constantly unlocking stuff\nGames plays very well, havent crashed or suffered any lag\n\nMIXED:\nMarble jumping is a little floaty/bouncy - sometimes this works well and adds to the enjoyment...sometimes its a little annoying to get through levels with it.\n\nCONS:\nWhen there are alot of \"wires\"  around, levels get a little messy\nsome levels are tough to follow or find the right direction.\n\nNote - I play with Mouse+Keyboard, I haven't tried the Xbox controller.\n\nOverall, If your looking for a simple indie game, you can't go wrong with this one.",
